sequenceDiagram
    participant V as Volcano Scheduler<br/>(Extender)
    participant C as Crater Backend<br/>(Informers)
    participant K as Kubernetes API Server

    Note over C,K: Informers maintain local object copies<br/>through List / Watch
    V->>C: Ask whether job A can be admitted during enqueue
    C->>C: Check platform rules using the<br/>admission snapshot and reservations
    C->>C: Checks pass, create a reservation for A
    C-->>V: Abstain: do not veto admission
    V->>V: Combine plugin results, update<br/>PodGroup state inside the Session
    Note over V,C: Continue with other candidates this cycle,<br/>Crater's checks include A's reservation

    V->>C: Call onSessionClose during Session cleanup
    C->>C: Invalidate the snapshot, keep reservations
    C-->>V: Return
    V->>K: Write back PodGroup admission status
    K-->>V: Write completed

    Note over V,K: Object cache synchronization and later admission checks<br/>advance independently, with no fixed ordering
    par Path 1: Watch synchronizes object state
        K--)C: Watch delivers object changes
        C->>C: Update the Informer object cache,<br/>the admission snapshot stays unchanged
    and Path 2: A later scheduling cycle sends an inquiry
        V->>C: Ask about the next admission candidate
        C->>C: Read the Informer cache and database settings,<br/>rebuild the admission snapshot
        C->>C: Reconcile A's reservation against the new snapshot
        alt The snapshot now counts A's requests
            C->>C: Remove A's reservation,<br/>snapshot accounting takes over
        else A's admission is unconfirmed<br/>and its reservation is unexpired
            C->>C: Keep A's reservation
        end
        C-->>V: Return a judgment using the new snapshot<br/>and remaining reservations
    end
